## Official-product IA/workflow benchmark — secondary evidence

This section is a comparison aid only. It does not replace any local-code truth, make a product-ready claim, or authorize an IA change.

| Official reference | Relevant product distinction | Audit implication for Marketing Hub |
|---|---|---|
| [Buffer — Scheduling posts](https://support.buffer.com/article/642-scheduling-posts) | One composer can select channels and generate channel-specific previews; it distinguishes Queue/Next Available, prioritized queue position, fixed date/time, and Now. | Keep Studio composition, per-channel state, queue, calendar and immediate/scheduled actions conceptually distinct; current Hub does **not** yet have one shared source/result model, so do not fake that continuity. |
| [Buffer — All Channels view](https://support.buffer.com/article/861-how-to-use-the-all-channels-view) | Cross-channel Draft, Approval, Queue and Sent views coexist with channel filtering; these are workflow views, not identical per-provider tabs. | Supports preserving the Hub’s distinct Inbox/Calendar route roles and provider-specific tabs instead of inventing a uniform provider shell. |
| [Later — Social Sets](https://help.later.com/hc/en-us/articles/360044369654-Create-Manage-Social-Sets) | An account grouping organizes connected profiles by brand/identity; access groups organize permissions and have their own media/calendar context. | Account/tenant truth should be a shared data concern across Studio, settings, and channel detail, but it does not justify renaming the existing customer sidebar or collapsing specialized surfaces. |
| [Later — Add, remove and transfer social profiles](https://help.later.com/hc/en-us/articles/360043244733-Add-Remove-Transfer-Social-Profiles-in-Later) | Profile authentication is a dedicated connection action reachable from Calendar or Settings. | Reinforces the current split between Studio creation and Settings/channel account connection; keep that split visible until a unified, proven contract exists. |
| [Hootsuite — Create and schedule content in a calendar](https://help.hootsuite.com/hc/de/articles/1260804306069-Create-and-schedule-content-in-a-calendar) | Calendar can expose post-level edit, delete, reschedule, approval and published-network access, with status changes. | Current `/calendar` is a read-only queue-derived date view; a prototype must not depict post-level recovery/result actions as already implemented. |
| [Hootsuite — Manage content calendar](https://help.hootsuite.com/hc/de/articles/1260804306009-Manage-your-content-calendar) | Calendar filtering is by account and post status, including draft/scheduled/published/failed/approval states. | If a future full Hub calendar adds these controls, it must be backed by one source of truth; it cannot be inferred from today’s queue view. |

**Benchmark conclusion:** established products separate (a) connected-account/permission organization, (b) composer and per-channel adaptation, (c) approval/queue/calendar workflow, and (d) analytics/inbox. This validates the audit’s preservation principle—do not force equal provider tabs—but does not validate any missing Marketing Hub bridge, result recovery, or provider capability.

